      "role": "user",
      "content": "so u're saying it's basically built into the culture? that sounds like a pretty heavy generalization. i've heard some people argue that these productivity gaps are less about \"culture\" and more about just being \"developing\" vs \"developed\" nations. but if we're talking strictly about the human element on the floor, are u saying that a worker in nigeria is inherently less likely to problem-solve on their own than a polish worker, regardless of their specific training?",
